{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 9.943,
   "text": "I took a winter job keeping an old lighthouse. The logbook had one rule, on the very first page."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 10.643,
   "end": 16.509,
   "text": "Keep the lamp turning. And if a light ever flashes back at you from the water... do not answer it."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 17.309,
   "end": 23.155,
   "text": "No boats come out in winter. It was just me, the wind, and the beam going round and round."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 23.855,
   "end": 30.937,
   "text": "On my ninth night, far past the rocks, a small light started blinking. Three short. Three long. Three short."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 31.537,
   "end": 33.031,
   "text": "S. O. S."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 35.031,
   "end": 40.855,
   "text": "I grabbed the signal lamp and aimed it at the water. My thumb was already on the switch."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 41.655,
   "end": 46.092,
   "text": "Then I flipped back through the logbook, looking for the coast guard's number."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 46.792,
   "end": 52.509,
   "text": "Every keeper before me had an entry for their ninth night. All of them said the same thing."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 53.109,
   "end": 55.819,
   "text": "Light on the water. Not answered."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 57.319,
   "end": 62.481,
   "text": "Every keeper... except the last one. His entry was just one word. Answered."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 63.481,
   "end": 67.471,
   "text": "Underneath, in shaky pencil: Someone is rowing in."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 69.071,
   "end": 73.039,
   "text": "There's nothing after that. Not one page. Until tonight."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 74.039,
   "end": 79.777,
   "text": "I haven't written a word tonight. But tonight's page is already filled in... in my handwriting."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start": 81.177,
   "end": 83.673,
   "text": "Answered. He's on the stairs."
  }
 ],
